# _redirects: read by BOTH Netlify and Cloudflare Pages. Use only what both support:
# plain 301/302/303/307/308 redirects and 200 rewrites to relative paths.
# Not allowed here: "!" force flags, 404 rules, query-parameter matching (Cloudflare has none of
# them). Netlify-only rules (the /api/* rewrite to Netlify Functions, hiding internal folders)
# live in netlify.toml, which Cloudflare ignores.
#
# Note the hosts differ: Cloudflare always applies a matching rule, Netlify skips a non-forced
# rule when a file exists at that path. So never add a rule whose path a real page could take.
# Rules are read top to bottom; the first match wins.
#
# Format: <from> <to> [status]   (Cloudflare limits: 2,000 static + 100 dynamic rules)

